% ============================================================================
% references.bib -- Scientific literature cited by the Atmospheric data
%                   Community Toolkit (ACT).
%
% Scope
%   Every work cited in a docstring "References" section across the act
%   package, plus three method sources cited in prose outside a formal
%   References block (ARM IRT Handbook, NOAA PSD-311 flux handbook, WMO
%   code tables).
%
% Provenance
%   Author lists, titles, volumes, pages and DOIs were resolved against
%   Crossref and DataCite where a record exists, so several entries below
%   are MORE complete (and in a few cases more correct) than the docstring
%   text they came from. Entries that could not be machine-verified carry
%   an explicit `note` saying so -- their fields reproduce the ACT
%   docstring verbatim and should be confirmed before use in a manuscript.
%
% Entry types
%   Software and dataset records use @misc (not the biblatex-only @software)
%   so the file parses under classic BibTeX as well as biblatex. Under
%   biblatex you may safely rewrite those four entries as @software.
%
% See references_by_module.rst for the reference-to-module/function map.
% ============================================================================


